{"availability":"available","full":"HexNinja555/opentakeoff","name":"opentakeoff","description":"Free, open-source PDF takeoff & estimating for flooring (and any trade) — open a plan, set the scale, trace areas with one-click room detection, add waste % and a materials buy list, then export your quantities. Runs entirely in your browser.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":7,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-20T20:59:47Z","updated":"2026-07-20T21:06:24Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://opentakeoff.netlify.app/","topics":["aec","blueprint","canvas","construction","construction-estimating","construction-tech","cost-estimation","estimating","flooring","flooring-takeoff","measurement","pdf","pdfjs","quantity-surveying","quantity-takeoff","react","self-hosted","takeoff","vite","webapp"],"demo":"https://opentakeoff.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.211Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.211Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.211Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.211Z","stars":7,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The first takeoff canvas built for people and AI agents.","New — July 2026: MCP server — your AI agent can drive the takeoff engine (npx opentakeoff-mcp, on the official MCP registry) — and browse the plan set natively: sheets, title-block text, and rendered pages as MCP resources (v0.2.0) · Provenance — every shape records how it was measured (its scale, one-click or hand-drawn, and person or agent) · One-Click Area traces hatched rooms and scanned plans · Marked Set PDF export — full changelog","OpenTakeoff is a free, open-source canvas for measuring quantities off a building plan — a takeoff. What makes it different is who can run it: a person or an AI agent, on the same engine. You click inside a room and it traces itself; an agent calls the same tool over MCP and gets the same number. And every measurement records how it was made — its scale, whether it was one-click or hand-drawn, and whether a person or an agent made it. The proof travels with the number."],"features":["Drag in a plan PDF, an image (a scan or a screenshot), or a whole .zip plan set straight off a bid platform. Zips are unpacked and images wrapped to PDF in your browser — multi-page and multi-sheet, with up to 4 sheets…","One-Click Area is the headline: click inside a room and the linework bounds it, the polygon traces itself, and the vertices snap to true corners. It reads the drawing the way an estimator does — hatching and poché don't…","Manual tracing gets a real drafting aid: 45°/90° angle lock. Come within a few degrees of square or diagonal and the segment you're drawing locks onto the axis — the click commits the locked point, so walls come out…","Auto-detects the drawn scale note off the sheet, or calibrate from any known dimension (click two points, type the real length). Scale is remembered per sheet — because plan sets are never one uniform scale, and tools…","A condition is one finish (LVP, carpet, tile, base, …). Each carries a line/fill color and a CAD hatch pattern (plank, herringbone, tile, terrazzo) so the canvas looks like the real drawing — plus a per-condition waste…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ffea83852eadca3368e3c5ecc8bc667cd8d2f60ad619521aa9aeab03a64d18e","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.345Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.345Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The first takeoff canvas built for people and AI agents.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The first takeoff canvas built for people and AI agents.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Free, open-source, and it runs in your browser — no account, no upload, no install.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No upload step, no conversion service, no account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"To self-host, it's one static build you can drop anywhere — there's no backend, no database, no environment to stand up.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8ffea83852eadca3368e3c5ecc8bc667cd8d2f60ad619521aa9aeab03a64d18e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.346Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-20T21:06:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexNinja555/opentakeoff/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T13:40:19.347Z","hash":"8ffea83852eadca3368e3c5ecc8bc667cd8d2f60ad619521aa9aeab03a64d18e","originalBytes":24754,"storedBytes":24754,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["scale","takeoff","mcp","plan","one","web","every","never","engine","same","capture","src","agent","opentakeoff","real","run","model","open","own","sheet","click","pdf","set","what","area","build","lib","live","materials","one-click","per","canvas","condition","plus","there","training","when","bid","estimating","flooring","geometry","layer","server","any","browser","data","drawing","each","export","nothing","npm","off","person","text","tool","vite","waste","angle","base","built","buy","commercial","demo","full","install","list","measurement","measuring","only","pages","readme.md","report","revision","sheets","static","work","app","before","button","contributing.md","count","coverage","deploy","docs","drawn","endpoint","exact","first","free","get","how","inside","linear","lines","measured","names","need","per-condition","point","quantity","room","rooms","runs","see","traces","type","against","border",